#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mul

#% text
# `mul(a, b, ...)` is the product `a*b*...`; the operator `*` writes it, and a number before a name may omit it (`2x`).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Products are kept in a canonical order and equal factors are collected into powers: `x*x` is `x^2`.

#% item
# A list argument multiplies element by element.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mul(2, 3, 4)
#% output
#= 24

#% cell
x*y*x
#% output
#= y*x^2

#% cell
[1, 2, 3]*[4, 5, 6]
#% output
#= [4, 10, 18]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A number times a list scales it:

#% cell
3*[1, 2, 3]
#% output
#= [3, 6, 9]

#% text
# Its head with `apply`:

#% cell
apply(mul, range(5))
#% output
#= 120

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `add`, `pow`, `product`, `dot`
